researchers are not surprised waste  water testing is emerging as a go-to  method for finding covet 19. developers  of alberta systems say it detects covert  19 up to a week before positive cases  are confirmed clinically making it a  valuable tool in pandemic response  for example the  reinstatement of masking in calgary that  decision was informed in part by  wastewater testing and that really shows  that wastewater testing can be part of  the evidence base that policy makers use  to make these critical decisions in how  we navigate the pandemic not surprising  when you consider the virus survives a  long time in the gastrointestinal tract  and samples are contributed unknowingly  by everyone when they go to the bathroom  i think what we've seen in alberta is  that this technology really works  we had to iron out some kinks like other  teams across canada and around the world  it seems smoothing out some kinks is  ongoing a team that developed a  wastewater testing system at dalhousie  university raised eyebrows by claiming  it found the omicron variant in halifax  in mid-november weeks before it was  publicly reported in nova scotia even  before it was reported by south africa  but nova scotia's top doctor was not  convinced we've actually had  conversations with the the researchers  and what it turned out they were  detecting the alpha variant they  actually weren't detecting omicron so  it's still a research tool that has yet  to be validated in many ways dalhousie  university says the school stands by  their team's finding a statement from  the nova scotia government says a  different sample suggests the presence  of omicron but the finding has not been  confirmed as those test results are  tested  calgary researchers are flushed with  success their findings are posted online  as real-time data showing concentrations  of covet in various parts of the city  with wastewater testing methods evolving  researchers hope it helps canada detect  more threats to public health in future  covert 19 or others  ross lord global news halifax
 

